  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: 82_Kalaw_FinalEvaluation
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Kalaw
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'SQUAWK!


    YOUR VOICE HAS BEEN HEARD!


    Look at how far you''ve
    come, traveler.


    You didn''t just memorize words.


    You learned to understand.
    You learned to respond. You learned to build your own sentences.


    You learned
    to ask for help, navigate the streets, introduce yourself, and communicate with
    the people of Ilocos.


    More importantly, you discovered that language lives
    through the people who speak it.


    Every word you learned came from someone.
    Every phrase carried a meaning. Every conversation connected you to the people
    and culture of this place.


    The language you practiced here is not simply
    something to collect.


    It is something living.


    Something carried by
    families, communities, traditions, and stories.


    Your journey through Vigan
    may be complete, but your journey with Ilokano does not have to end here.


    The
    more you listen, the more you speak. The more you speak, the more you understand.


    And
    the more you understand, the closer you become to the people and culture that
    keep this language alive.


    Great job, traveler.


    You''ve taken another
    step in restoring the voices of the regions.'
  translatedText: 
  animationTrigger: 
  triggerEventName: 
  endEventName: 'SetObjective: Ilocos Chapter Complete'
  choices: []
